          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em inductive type
            is…
          %p
            In terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            %em inductive type
            is a type whose interpretation is given by an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra+of+an+endofunctor"} initial algebra of an endofunctor
          %p
            This has the usual meaning in ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+space"} contractible space
            of choices (as discussed at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} initial object in an (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntax
            will give back the traditional meaning whenever equality is interpreted
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theory"} extensionally
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are two
            %em equivalent
            ways of defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgement"} judgement
            rules for inductive types. The first describes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+elimination"} elimination
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+types"} dependent types
            over the given type. This is the formalization of the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
          %ul
