          %h3#CategoricalSemantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of inductive types.
          #InterpretationOfTheRules.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The categorical interpretation of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction"} induction
              %em dependent elimination
              and computation rules from
              %a{:href => "#InductionRules"} above
              are the following.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ambient+category"} ambient category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+introduction+rule"} term introduction rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of inductive term introduction is by an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
                  and an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"} algebra over an endofunctor
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi W
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F(W) \to W
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+elimination+rule"} term elimination rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of the dependent elimination rule says that given a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/display+map"} display map
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo →
                          %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to W
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                  is given an
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"} algebra structure
                  and the display map is an
                  = succeed "-algebra" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mo :
                          %mi W
                          %mo →
                          %mi B
                          %mo ∈
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi W
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : W \to B \in \mathcal{C}_{/W}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi W
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi σ
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi B
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi id
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi W
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        W
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\overset{\sigma}{\longrightarrow}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        B
                        \\\
                        \&amp;
                        {}_{\mathllap{id}}\searrow
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\swarrow_{\mathrlap{}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        W
                        }
                %p
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rule"} computation rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of the dependent computation rules is that the section
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  from above is required to be an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"} algebra
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
          #InterpretationOfTheSimpleRules.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The categorical interpretation of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursion
              %a{:href => "#RecursionRules"} above
              in a suitable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is the following
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+introduction+rule"} term introduction rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of inductive term introduction is by an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
                  and an
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"} algebra over an endofunctor
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi W
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi W
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F(W) \to W
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term+elimination+rule"} term elimination rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of the absolute elimination rule is that for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  any other
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+an+endofunctor"} algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to A
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/computation+rule"} computation rule
                %p
                  The interpretation of the absolute computation rule says that the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi W
                        %mo →
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to A
                  from above is an algebra
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
                  and is unique as such.
            %p
              In summary this says that the recursion rules are interpreted as an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra+of+an+endofunctor"} initial algebra of an endofunctor
          #BothFormulationsOfInitialityAreEquivalent.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              When interpreted in a category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type"} homotopy 0-types
              \= sets, definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InterpretationOfTheRules"}
              and definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InterpretationOfTheSimpleRules"}
              are indeed equivalent.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is an initial
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InterpretationOfTheSimpleRules"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initiality
              entails first of all the existence of a morphims to any other object it follows that with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              another
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to W
              the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to B \to W
              has to equal the identity
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_W
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \to W
              has a section, and uniquely so.
            %p
              Conversely, assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              satisfies definition
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InterpretationOfTheRules"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              any other
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \times A \to W
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              of this is equivalently just a morphism
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              to any other
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              is an initial
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f, g : W \to A
              two algebra homomorphism, they are necessarily equal.
            %p
              To that end, notice that by the assumption of 0-truncation, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta \colon A \to A \times A
              is a display map / fibration.
            %p
              Form its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi δ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi W
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %mi f
                                %mo ,
                                %mi g
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                            %mo ×
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    P &amp; \to &amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^\mathrlap{\delta}
                    \\\
                    W &amp; \underset{\langle f, g \rangle}{\to} &amp; A \times A,
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is also an algebra homomorphism. Therefore by the interpretation of the elimination rule it has a (specified)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo :
                      %mi W
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : W \to P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to W
              is the pullback of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              and therefore itself a monomorphism, and so the section forces it to be in fact an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are equal.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+object"} path object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P A \to A \times A
              (represented in type theory by an
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              are homotopic. A fancier version of this argument enables us to show that the space of algebra maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W\to A
              is actually contractible. In other words, the axioms for an inductive type still imply that algebra maps out of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              are essentially unique, even though the axioms do not state this explicitly.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#homotopy_initiality Homotopy initiality
          %p
            Any inductive type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is a homotopy initial F-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+endofunctor"}> algebra
            \: the space of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+an+endofunctor"} algebra
            maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \to X
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
          %p
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#AwodeyGambinoSojakova12"}> Awodey, Gambino &amp; Sojakova (2012)
            \&amp;rbrack;
          %h2#Examples Examples
          %blockquote
            %p
