            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+type"}> positive type
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+type"} negative type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive+type"}> higher inductive type
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+algebra+of+a+presentable+%E2%88%9E-monad"} initial algebra of a presentable ∞-monad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coinductive+type"} coinductive type
          %h2#References References
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesHistoryOfInductiveTypes History of inductive types
            %p
              Historical references on the definition of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
            %h4#precursors Precursors
            %p
              A first
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theoretic
              formulation of general
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+definitions"} inductive definitions
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Hauptsatz for the Intuitionistic Theory of Iterated Inductive Definitions
                %strong 63
                (1971) 179-216
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(08)70847-4"} doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(08)70847-4
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/induction+principle"} induction principle
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
              (also known as “path induction” or the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-rule"}> J-rule
              ”) is first stated in:
            %ul
              %li#MartinLof75
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
                , §1.7 and p. 94 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An intuitionistic theory of types: predicative part
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Logic Colloquium ‘73, Proceedings of the Logic Colloquium
                %strong 80
                (1975) 73-118 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1"}> doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(08)71945-1
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.131.926"} CiteSeer
            %p
              and in the modern form of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
              in:
            %ul
              %li{:id => "NordströmPeterssonSmith90"}
                Bengt Nordström, Kent Petersson, Jan M. Smith, §8.1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Programming in Martin-Löf’s Type Theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/research/group/logic/book/"} webpage
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cse.chalmers.se/research/group/logic/book/book.pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/NordstromPeterssonSmith-TypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p
              The special case of inductive types now known as
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/W-types"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒲
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{W}
                  \-types
              is first formulated in:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
                  , pp. 171 of:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Constructive Mathematics and Computer Programming
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Proceedings of the Sixth International Congress of Logic, Methodology and Philosophy of Science (1979)
                  %strong 104
                  (1982) 153-175
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0049-237X(09)70189-2"} doi:10.1016/S0049-237X(09)70189-2
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/studies-in-logic-and-the-foundations-of-mathematics/vol/104/suppl/C"} ISBN:978-0-444-85423-0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"} Per Martin-Löf
                  (notes by
                  = succeed ")," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Intuitionistic type theory
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://archive-pml.github.io/martin-lof/pdfs/Bibliopolis-Book-retypeset-1984.pdf"} pdf
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/MartinLofIntuitionisticTypeTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %p Early proposals for a general formal definition of inductive types:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+L.+Constable"}> Robert L. Constable
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N.+Paul+Francis+Mendler"} N. Paul Francis Mendler
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Recursive definitions in type theory
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Logic of Programs 1985
                  %strong 193
                  Springer (1985)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-15648-8_5"} doi:10.1007/3-540-15648-8_5
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Francis+Mendler"}> Paul Francis Mendler
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Inductive Definition in Type Theory
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  %a{:href => "https://hdl.handle.net/1813/6710"} hdl:1813/6710
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roland+Backhouse"}> Roland Backhouse
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em On the Meaning and Construction of the Rules of Martin-Löf’s Theory of Types
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/88/ECS-LFCS-88-52/"} Workshop on General Logic
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://www.bcs.org/media/5076/bcs-facs-martin-lof-theory-of-types-a-computing-scientists-perspective-roland-backhouse-sep1987-file-4.pdf"} pdf
                  %a{:href => "http://www.lfcs.inf.ed.ac.uk/reports/88/ECS-LFCS-88-52/ECS-LFCS-88-52.pdf"} pdf
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %h4#modern_definition Modern definition
            %p
              The modern notion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+families"} inductive families
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theory"} intensional type theory
              is independently due to
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Dybjer"}> Peter Dybjer
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em Inductive sets and families in Martin-Löf’s type theory and their set-theoretic semantics
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511569807.012"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511569807.012
                  %a{:href => "http://www.cse.chalmers.se/~peterd/papers/Setsem_Inductive.pdf"} pdf
